#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e02202-ebdf-5987-bbaf-b5eb204c3892" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Radical Function With an Even Index"}] :question/id #uuid "7096f867-7d37-5630-a885-d0a4f4a6acb7" :question/math-academy-id "e-8142" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x) = -2\\sqrt[4]{1-2x}+1?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\sqrt[4] x$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4] x \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{1-2x} \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-2$ and then adding $1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{1-2x} & \\ge 0 \\\\ -2\\sqrt[4]{1-2x} & \\le 0 \\\\ -2\\sqrt[4]{1-2x}+1 & \\le 1 \\\\ f(x) & \\le 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x) \\in (-\\infty,1].$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/3c/3ce03253fe40abe25d69866d5b52a621168e3dab2a45ca33d951f1a4551b98c9.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179546 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abc2f98-9bbd-5a33-87fc-f9459fb18c60" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Radical Function With an Odd Index"}] :question/id #uuid "9af3bd0c-c209-508f-b806-bb9426f2c0da" :question/math-academy-id "e-8719" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x) = -3\\sqrt[3]{5-2x}+6?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $y = \\sqrt[3] x$ is\n$y \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nTransformations do not change this interval. Therefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $y \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abc2f98-9bbd-5a33-87fc-f9459fb18c60" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Radical Function With an Odd Index"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4c0c2e7-a681-5895-ba10-ff483e0d39c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4c0c2e7-a681-5895-ba10-ff483e0d39c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566720} :answer-field/id #uuid "093964bd-ff38-5f0e-86cf-44fda5192e70" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c7c6cee-5f26-5163-aef9-b6c2c21fef72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c7c6cee-5f26-5163-aef9-b6c2c21fef72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566669} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b586c24-5829-583a-853a-6e1f725764ae" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d71d3ff-673f-5af8-856b-f4fba51d797e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d71d3ff-673f-5af8-856b-f4fba51d797e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566542} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec880312-644c-50f1-b24c-6e466f7d3706" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc1be539-2c57-57bf-8551-1be15ab433cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-276500" :question/problem "What is the range of $f(x)=\\sqrt[7]{4x+12}-25?$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "The range of $y=\\sqrt[7]{x}$ is\n$-\\infty <y<\\infty .$\nTransformations do not change this interval. Therefore, the range of the given function is \n\n$$\n-\\infty <f(x)<\\infty .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e02202-ebdf-5987-bbaf-b5eb204c3892" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Radical Function With an Even Index"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56805b6e-2be8-5be9-b9aa-949f59554901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56805b6e-2be8-5be9-b9aa-949f59554901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566526} :answer-field/id #uuid "812660c1-6e58-5fde-a9eb-cdbacccb3d5d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566938} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c32565a-624d-5444-98d2-b0e525f09e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c32565a-624d-5444-98d2-b0e525f09e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566668} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5c16641-aad5-5aa7-8298-3b4fbdb5bdb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24c95c95-c540-5c0a-8194-316e0ede5671" :question/math-academy-id "q-276694" :question/problem "What is the range of $h(x)=-4\\sqrt[4]{5x+2}?$\n\n$h(x)\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\sqrt[4]{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{5x+2}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{5x+2} & \\ge 0 \\\\ -4\\sqrt[4]{5x+2} & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is \n$h(x)\\in (-\\infty ,0].$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=h(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/88/887a12a283f56e3ea61c29ff57145f32663831a3eb9ab470c51e8cd33e5b2ede.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3abc2f98-9bbd-5a33-87fc-f9459fb18c60" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Radical Function With an Odd Index"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3671ae60-6fe3-5ef7-8908-5ee328bc5f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566470} {:answer/id #uuid "5b46d4da-dd36-56f0-933a-b5752b8ff85e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566538} {:answer/id #uuid "64108857-c661-5b43-a2ed-e249edf5c09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566555} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b3b7f2-d52c-5562-b8c6-9bdebd81e462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-5,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566786} {:answer/id #u